From: Fix <dev@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:32:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Light/dark themes: tokens, switch, contrast-checked
 palette for every screen

- theme.css: one token table for light + dark (dark = the original colours); switch in the sidebar and on sign-in; remembers the choice, follows the system
- Classic constants and accent colours now use the tokens (dark mode unchanged apart from brightening the dimmest helper text, which was 2.4:1 contrast)
- Workspace screens: 467 hard-coded colours turned into role-based variables; light = exact originals; dark mapped by role/lightness
- Tests: contrast of core tokens in both themes; every text-on-background pair in the workspace source in dark mode (61 pairs); light mode identical to before
- Map markers re-resolve their colours on theme change; dark map tiles
- docs/UNIFIED_WORKSPACE.md; acceptance checklist section 8
